{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqgtiljwcn2","workspace":"D:\\zonoid","title":"Codex-parity feature: usage pricing design (pricing.json consumed by adapter; add-dollar overlay)","summary":"Decomposed Codex adapter hardening into feature orch/feature/codex-parity with 3 independent impl tasks (disjoint file sets): CDX-1 gate apply_patch worktree confinement, CDX-2 installer Claude+Codex coexistence, CDX-3 Codex usage accounting + dollar pricing. Two design choices LOCKED for CDX-3, user-endorsed: (A) per-model rate tables live in a shipped pricing.json that the ADAPTERS consume — pricing logic and the price(slice) method stay adapter-owned, the daemon only SUMS cost.usd subtotals and propagates the weakest source flag; rate data sits in config so a price change is an edit not a release. (B) ADD a dollar overlay derived from by_model, keeping TOKENS as the source of truth — do not replace the token-based costflow/autonomy math. Linchpin finding that makes real (not just estimated) Codex token capture possible: Codex emits a turn.completed event carrying a usage dict (OpenAI Responses shape) in its --json stream and interactive session rollout under ~/.codex/sessions — proven by featurebench codex.py:138-146 which fails a run if that usage block is missing. Estimate (chars/4 + source:'estimated' flag) is only the fallback when the usage event is absent.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-16T15:49:46.268Z","vec":[-0.14278072118759155,0.003237302415072918,-0.04036865010857582,0.016726890578866005,0.020351676270365715,-0.09264446794986725,-0.002383634215220809,0.08860908448696136,0.05959843471646309,0.03977048024535179,0.033435311168432236,-0.0822237879037857,0.0029123672284185886,-0.04043279588222504,0.06804159283638,-0.004264639690518379,0.02226370759308338,0.022824062034487724,-0.06683836132287979,-0.007570105139166117,0.04761684313416481,-0.06628447026014328,-0.048166271299123764,0.009442897513508797,0.010805263184010983,0.009994051419198513,0.009758977219462